{"path":"atomic/atomic/load","title":"std::atomic<T>::load","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::atomic&lt;T&gt;::</span>load","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic/load","section":"atomic","kind":"page","summary":"Atomically loads and returns the current value of the atomic variable. Memory is affected according to the value of order.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">T load<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">T load<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">volatile</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Atomically loads and returns the current value of the atomic variable. Memory is affected according to the value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">order</span></code>.\n</p><p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">order</span></code> is one of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2117\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_release</span></span></a></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2118\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_acq_rel</span></span></a></span></code>, the behavior is undefined.\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-cxx20\"><td>\n<p>It is deprecated if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic\"><span class=\"kw2083\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atomic</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_always_lock_free</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> and overload <span class=\"t-v\">(2)</span> participates in overload resolution.\n</p>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> order\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> memory order constraints to enforce\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The current value of the atomic variable.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic/operator_T\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator T</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  loads a value from an atomic object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_load\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atomic_load</span><span>atomic_load_explicit</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  atomically obtains the value stored in an atomic object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"atomic","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"atomic/atomic","title":"std::atomic"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::atomic<T>::load","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++11. Atomically loads and returns the current value of the atomic variable."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"order"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The current value of the atomic variable."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"operator T","note":"loads a value from an atomic object"},{"label":"atomic_load, atomic_load_explicit","note":"atomically obtains the value stored in an atomic object"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":116,"codeBlockCount":0}
